    "turn_idx": 81,
    "turn_text": "We did, as I sit here and think about it, what it brings back to mind was, or is the contract with America. I can't tell you, because I don't have a great memory, sitting here at this moment, if it was one of the 10 items in the contract with America, but I think it was. I'd have to pull out a copy and I'll try to make myself do that when I get home. The contract for the miracle was, in some ways, great for the nation, but it was also, in some ways, great for the freshman class. Because if you have a change in the majority, and you get there by pledging reform, the standard for politicians is to talk about reform and never do reform. But because Newt had come up with the idea And then really done a lot of work in the time span between 1992 and 1994. When we ran on the contract, they worked hard, I mean long hours, developing the contract. But once they had produced it, and I have one of my best friends in the Congress was a member who had been elected in 92, two years ahead of me. And he had worked hard on developing it. But it was a blueprint that we could hold the old bulls too.",
